   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Consider the curve given by \\( xy^{2} + x^{2} = 5 \\), along which \\( y \\) is a differentiable function of \\( x \\) near the point \\( (1, 2) \\). Find the value of \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} \\) at the point \\( (1, 2) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         11,
         8
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Differentiate \\( xy^{2} + x^{2} = 5 \\) implicitly with respect to \\( x \\): \\( 2 x + y^{2} + \\left(2 x y\\right)\\frac{dy}{dx} = 0 \\), so \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = - \\frac{1}{y} - \\frac{y}{2 x} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  1,
                  "y"
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Negate",
               [
                  "Divide",
                  "y",
                  [
                     "Multiply",
                     2,
                     "x"
                  ]
               ]
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Differentiate \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{- 2 x - y^{2}}{2 x y} \\) again with the quotient rule, treating \\( y \\) as a function of \\( x \\): \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = \\frac{2 x y \\left(- 2 \\frac{dy}{dx} y - 2\\right) - \\left(- 2 x - y^{2}\\right) \\left(2 \\frac{dy}{dx} x + 2 y\\right)}{4 x^{2} y^{2}} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            -3,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( (1, 2) \\), \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = - \\frac{3}{2} \\). Substitute this value and the coordinates into the second derivative.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            11,
            8
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = \\frac{11}{8} \\) at \\( (1, 2) \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            11,
            8
         ]
      }
   ],
